Third-party components and attribution
================================================================================

1. Hugging Face Transformers — Apache License 2.0
   https://github.com/huggingface/transformers

   `src/ccl/rope.py` imports `rotate_half` from
   `transformers.models.qwen3.modeling_qwen3`, and its `apply_rope_to_keys`
   deliberately mirrors the key half of that module's `apply_rotary_pos_emb`
   so that re-applied rotary embeddings are bit-compatible with the model's own.
   `src/ccl/target.py` and `src/ccl/compress.py` use the public `Cache` /
   `DynamicCache` API.

   The extraction pass in `src/ccl/compressor.py` reproduces the arithmetic of
   `Qwen3Attention.forward` and `Qwen3DecoderLayer.forward` (q_norm/k_norm before
   RoPE, GQA key/value repetition, o_proj, the post-attention MLP residual) so
   that memory tokens flow through the frozen target's own layers. It was written
   against the published module and is a reimplementation, not a verbatim copy.

