================================================================================
Research attribution — methods reproduced, not code copied
================================================================================

The compressor implemented here is a reimplementation of the *published
mechanism* of C²KV. No source code from the C²KV project was copied, consulted
line-by-line, or vendored; the implementation was written from the paper's
description of its structured attention flow, its shared compression-token
embedding, its per-layer QKV projection heads, and its pre-RoPE storage with
positional reassignment at composition time.

  C²KV: Compressed and Composable KV Cache Reuse for Efficient LLM Inference
  Du, Chen, Tang, Liu, Lan, Qu, Niu, Liu, Chen, Wu. KDD 2026.
  arXiv:2607.17715 — https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.17715
  Reference implementation (not used here): https://github.com/s7a9/C2KV

Other work whose ideas informed the experimental design, with no code reused,
is credited in `docs/RELATED_WORK.md`, which separates published prior art (§5)
from what this repository actually measured (§6) and the remaining gaps (§7).

================================================================================
Data
================================================================================

Every corpus in `results/raw/corpus/` and `results/stage3/` is **synthetic** and
generated deterministically by `src/ccl/corpus.py` and `src/ccl/stage3_corpus.py`
from explicit integer seeds. It contains no scraped text, no personal data, and
no third-party copyrighted material. Entity names, hosts and paths are invented
and any resemblance to real systems is coincidental.

Known cosmetic issue: three of the four synthetic hostnames use RFC 2606 reserved
domains (`depot.example.net`, `relay.example.org`, `vault.example.com`), but the
draw-B pool also contains `gateway.example.io`, and `.io` is not reserved. These
strings are inert — they are answers in a question-answering corpus and are never
requested over the network by any code in this repository. It is left uncorrected
because `src/ccl/corpus.py` is covered by the Stage 3 integrity hashes in
`results/stage3/freeze.json`; changing it would invalidate the frozen provenance
of a completed held-out evaluation, which is a worse outcome than an imperfect
example domain.
